# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
# `/node_modules` is anchored to the repo root, so a nested one is NOT covered:
# voice-gateway/node_modules appeared (vite cache) and was untracked-but-unignored,
# one broad `git add -A` away from committing a dependency tree.
/node_modules
voice-gateway/node_modules/
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage

# next.js
/.next/
/out/

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# local Claude preview/dev config
.claude/
__pycache__/
*.log
wake-diag.log

# ── Personal Config: real profile data stays LOCAL ───────────────────────────
# "Private repo" is not the same as "not exposed": history is permanent, a push
# or a shared branch leaks it, and a later .gitignore does not undo a commit.
# Tracked: schema, loader, synthetic *.example.yaml. Never: Roei's own data.
voice-gateway/profiles/*.yaml
!voice-gateway/profiles/*.example.yaml

# ── Knowledge-extraction raw artifacts: LOCAL BACKUP, never tracked ──────────
# The harvest/journal payloads quote source material verbatim — political,
# family-loyalty, dating and biographical excerpts — and carry ~284 absolute
# local paths. The synthesis neutralises that content; the raw layer does not.
# A local backup and a git history are different needs: this survives the loss
# of ~/cluod code (which has no remote) without entering permanent history.
# Tracked instead: the consolidated report and a sanitized manifest.
#
# `raw/*` not `raw/` — git never descends into an excluded DIRECTORY, so the
# .gitkeep negation below would be dead with the directory form.
docs/knowledge-inventory/raw/*
!docs/knowledge-inventory/raw/.gitkeep

# ── Merlin storage roots: machine-local paths, never tracked ─────────────────
# storage_root -> absolute base is a fact about ONE laptop. The example is
# committed so the shape is discoverable; the real map is not.
voice-gateway/config/storage_roots.yaml
voice-gateway/config/storage_roots.json
